<title>Switzerland: ACI says Dec 1996 world air cargo up 6.7pct.</title>
<headline>ACI says Dec 1996 world air cargo up 6.7pct.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic handled</p>
<p>by 487 airports around the world in December 1996, totalled 4,481,458 million tonnes, up 6.7 percent on the same month the previous year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in ACI's six geographical regions in tonnes during December 1996, with percentage change on December 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>				December 1996	Percent Change on</p>
<p>December 1995</p>
<p> Africa			  48,957			up     26.9 percent</p>
<p> Asia/Pacific		 961,293			up     11.3</p>
<p> Europe			 906,330			up	5.3</p>
<p> L.America/Carribean	117,617			up     17.1</p>
<p> Middle East		  147,732			up     15.9</p>
<p> North America	    2,299,529			up	4.0</p>
<p>	  Total	     4,481,458			up	6.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
